{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/142785-sell-me-on-demon","id":142785,"title":"Sell me on Demon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-19T17:14:07-07:00","id":142785,"title":"Sell me on Demon","content":"As the title sort of suggests, I am apprehensive when it comes to purchasing D:TD for a couple of reasons. Most of those reasons however are all related to the fact that the World of Darkness already has established books such as Inferno which deal with demons as a whole including powers, contracts, etc.<br /> <br /> When D:TD was released, it seems that all of the previous works done with Inferno as well as much of their lore was undone. They are no longer entities from hell who are under the purveyance of vices and seek to be evil simply for the sake that they ARE evil.<br /> <br /> Now, demons are fallen angels of the God Machine and are constantly on the run from it and the angel servants. They no longer are the embodiment of evil simply because they are demons, but angels who simply couldn't perform the duties the God Machine wished of them and hence now on the run from it.<br /> <br /> Is there any way to keep the demons of old while still using the book of D:TD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T17:26:54-07:00","id":142810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/142785-sell-me-on-demon#post142785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When D:TD was released, it seems that all of the previous works done with Inferno as well as much of their lore was undone. They are no longer entities from hell who are under the purveyance of vices and seek to be evil simply for the sake that they ARE evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so! In fact, the book has a big section that addresses exactly this concern:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: The Descent, p. 23</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>DEMONS, DEMONS, DEMONS</b><br /> <br /> In the years since the <b>World of Darkness Rulebook</b> was released, the game lines supporting it have detailed a great many entities referred to as \u201cdemons.\u201d One or two of them actually were demons as <b>Demon: The Descent</b> describes them, but most weren\u2019t.<br /> <br /> This game doesn\u2019t make those books \u201cnot count.\u201d The World of Darkness has room for all sorts of malevolent otherworldly beings that a mortal witness can call a demon. The majority of these creatures have nothing to do with the God-Machine and wouldn\u2019t mistake the Unchained for their own kind, and the Unchained in turn don\u2019t mistake them for fellow Fallen angels.<br /> <br /> The many entities known as demons include:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The inhabitants of the Inferno, seen in <b>World of Darkness: Inferno</b>, are vice-eating malevolent spirits that tempt humanity to sin. Probably the most-developed \u201cdemons\u201d other than the Unchained, references to \u201cmaejlin\u201d in <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b> or some references to \u201cthe Lower Depths\u201d in <b>Mage: The Awakening</b> refer to these entities.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Imps and Wraiths of Pandemonium, living symbols of Space and Mind seen in <b>Mage: The Awakening</b>, are called \u201cdemons\u201d by the mages who encounter them during their Awakening visions.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Still with Mage, mages who explore the astral realms within their souls encounter demon-like representations of their own moral weaknesses, the \u201cgoetic demons.\u201d Some mages summon these entities into the world as servants.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Lucifuge, an organization of hunters in <b>Hunter: The Vigil</b>, claim to be descended from demons described as being much closer to the Miltonian, classical, Judeo-Christian demon myths than any of the other entities seen here.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The fae of <b>Changeling: The Lost</b> sometimes encounter creatures who claim to be demons while wandering in the dreams of humanity.<br /> <br /> \u2022 And, finally, <b>Demon: The Descent</b> demons. A few appear in <b>Promethean: The Created</b> and its line. One cameos in <b>World of Darkness: Midnight Roads</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, to answer your question, you can have any kind of demon you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 05-19-2014, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T17:34:02-07:00","id":142822,"title":"","content":"Demon: the Descent doesn't undo anything. The Inferno is still there. There are dominions that come out of it and diaboli that are touched by its iniquity. These things feed on vice and iniquity and whisper within the human soul to drag it down with them. These are things which can be called demons.<br /> <br /> Demon: the Descent presents a legion of infrastructural angels, as well as the fallen angels who turn from the choir to their own selfish ends and bargain for human souls in exchange for temporal power. These are also things which can be called demons.<br /> <br /> They're not the same things, any more than Mage is talking about diaboli from the Inferno when it speaks of the supernal demons of Pandemonium, for example.<br /> <br /> If you want to run the dominions of vice and iniquity and the hosts of Hell from World of Darkness: Inferno, use World of Darkness: Inferno. If you want to look into reading Demon: the Descent, my advice is to put the Inferno aside, remember that it will still be there when you are done reading, and open your mind to a different type of game with different themes and feels to it. Descent is an excellent book in my opinion, with themes of identity, deception, and a tight emotional connection to the world around you, enough that you would tear yourself away from union with God to dwell in the muck with the sinners. If you read it expecting to hit the same notes as Inferno, though, you'll be barking up the wrong tree; that book already exists and you already own it, why sell it to you a second time?<br /> <br /> You don't have to purchase it sight-unseen, by the way. The Kickstarter for the deluxe print edition of Demon: the Descent is over, but it included an official, non-pirated link to a near-final version of the manuscript before layout and artwork that is very close to the full final text of the book. <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7FqViticwNueVdxTmVNTjE0MTQ/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Read Demon: the Descent here</a> and decide for yourself whether it's worth your money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T17:48:24-07:00","id":142830,"title":"","content":"The above assumptions are mistaken. They're even addressed in the corebook itself. Unchained have absolutely nothing to do with Dominions and other Demonic entities depicted in Inferno, and what's more, they could share the same setting with minor revisions to the Inferno ruleset as to integrate it to the GMC appendix.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T18:15:05-07:00","id":142877,"title":"","content":"That definitely helps since a huge issue was feeling like Inferno would be invalidated when they present some of the most interesting antagonists in the game.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, now that that is sorted out, what is the main feel of D:TD? I understand you are on the run from the God Machine, but what do you try to do on the whole? Werewolves patrol and uphold the legacy of Father Wolf, Changelings want to reclaim lost humanity, etc. Demons...hide? Tempt people to sin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T18:19:37-07:00","id":142893,"title":"","content":"Depends on your own agendas.. some Demons fight God-Machine.. other's want to reintegrate with it.. others still just want to live for themselves. On the whole tho, it's about hiding, spying, gathering info and doing something with it. Whenever it's for your own protection or for your own gain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T18:36:25-07:00","id":142899,"title":"","content":"Heck, once the Demon Translation Guide comes out, you may have ANOTHER class of Demons to play with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T18:45:05-07:00","id":142928,"title":"","content":"Last week my Demon: the Descent character orchestrated the attempted murder of an angel undercover in the local police department, while simultaneously creating an urgent false alarm to direct the entire rest of the police force to the secret warehouse laboratory the angel was in place to keep secret, all from the safety of her own home. The week before she nearly got her best friend and herself killed by one of the creatures the laboratory was experimenting with, and has to deal with the fact that now he knows that, while she looks like a nerdy scenester college girl, she is actually a cloud of flying, stinging quicksilver globules.<br /> <br /> Demons, like changelings, are at a disadvantage: a vast enemy is lurking out there, and they are prime prey for it should it turn its attention their way. Demons, therefore, each have an individual vision of a Hell of their own to reign in, safe from the destroying angels of Heaven, whether that vision consists of the obliteration of the enemy, escape to a safe refuge, or the machine-satori necessary to understand how to effortlessly move between the raindrops and escape God's notice. Demons come with an in-built character hook: the Fall is not because they &quot;simply could not perform their duties,&quot; but always originates, consciously or not, in some feeling or frustration or decision of their own. Every demon Fell for a reason, and every Fall's catalyst is unique and tells us what your character cares about in the world, whether that be people she loves, foes she hates, pleasures she refuses to surrender, freedom to make her own mark on the world independent of another, or even simple attachment to an aesthetic, philosophy or way of life. There was something you cared about enough to spit in God's face when he told you to give it up. If there wasn't, you wouldn't be Unchained.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, there are spy-thriller games of intrigue and questions of identity. A demon can maintain multiple Cover identities and may identify with them to differing degrees, seeing one identity as an honest representation of himself or viewing all of them as tools and disguises that hide his true demonic self. The demon must keep up appearances and find ways to achieve his goals without acting grossly out of character for the identity he is wearing, or else his protective Cover degrades, and ultimately, he is found out by the Machine and it responds and sends antibodies. A demon who plays this game can play it well, though; a demon in deep Cover is arguably as invisible in the crowd as a changeling, or moreso. Demons have complete control of their emotional expressions and body language, making them consummate liars and actors.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the only way to improve degraded Covers is to either convince human beings to sign away parts of their lives\u2014relationships, jobs, acquaintences, hobbies\u2014for you to take and patch into one of your Covers; to convince them to sell you the right to claim their immortal soul as raw materials to reweave as that person's entire life and identity, now nothing more than a coat you can don or doff, stepping into his life and claiming it for yourself; or to <i>fucking wrestle an angel and eat it.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T18:57:42-07:00","id":142936,"title":"","content":"Wow that is one doozy of a life, but I do like the fact that they are similar to changelings in the whole hunted aspect. Are the unchained crossover friendly? Or do they steal the show when used?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T19:08:27-07:00","id":142944,"title":"","content":"Demon powers are fancy and cosmic, and they have access to a few tricks other supernaturals would gawk at, like going loud (a desperation move\u2014destroy an entire identity permanently, burning it for fuel for a single scene's worth of phenomenal power, like we're talking their power stat and fuel pool temporarily max out levels of power). Additionally, the curve bends weirdly, as a demon who pursues his Cipher assiduously can gain, in the ascent to unlocking a personal mystic secret, a couple extra powers and dots of their power stat earlier than most other supernaturals would. They have nothing like the Promethean's Disquiet, the mummy's death cycle or the vampire's daysleep that would intrinsically interfere with adventuring together in a practical sense. Balance is imprecise, but that's always an issue with crossover. (And in fairness, they have some drawbacks other supernaturals don't face, too\u2014their fuel stat is relatively scarce until they hit high Primum, and they have no innate means of healing quickly without specific powers, not even external resources like changelings' goblin fruits or stopgaps like Sin-Eaters' plasm reinforcement.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T19:18:27-07:00","id":142956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/142785-sell-me-on-demon?p=142928#post142928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and the only way to improve degraded Covers is to either convince human beings to sign away parts of their lives\u2014relationships, jobs, acquaintences, hobbies\u2014for you to take and patch into one of your Covers; to convince them to sell you the right to claim their immortal soul as raw materials to reweave as that person's entire life and identity, now nothing more than a coat you can don or doff, stepping into his life and claiming it for yourself; or to <i>fucking wrestle an angel and eat it.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Or, and this one is the doozy given that your former master's nigh-omnipresence in the mortal sphere will forever tempt you away from it, you can eschew the glory of your mightiest powers and live the lie you claim is your life <i>so well </i>that you<i> <b>deceive the universe</b></i><i>.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T20:48:44-07:00","id":142998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/142785-sell-me-on-demon?p=142956#post142956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, and this one is the doozy given that your former master's nigh-omnipresence in the mortal sphere will forever tempt you away from it, you can eschew the glory of your mightiest powers and live the lie you claim is your life <i>so well </i>that you<i> <b>deceive the universe</b></i><i>.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>But the only one you can't deceive is yourself. That's the cross every Unchained bears. &quot;Are these my feelings? Or just how I was programmed to be eons ago? And if so... Did God knew I would eventually Fall?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T01:40:36-07:00","id":143195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/142785-sell-me-on-demon?p=142877#post142877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I understand you are on the run from the God Machine, but what do you try to do on the whole? Werewolves patrol and uphold the legacy of Father Wolf, Changelings want to reclaim lost humanity, etc. Demons...hide? Tempt people to sin?</div> </div> </div> </div>DtD probably has the most drive baked directly into the system that makes the PCs proactively involved in the world. Just by beind a Demon that wants to survive there is a lot of stuff you should be doing. Someone on another board once summed it up pretty well:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacobkosh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The recently-kickstarted DEMON: THE DESCENT is a terrific read, something I am super-looking forweard to playing, and also possibly a signpost toward how Onyx Path/White Wolf are addressing this issue. The game still gives you a lot of open-ended freedom, but there's also an antagonist and a natural source of conflict baked right into the system and the mechanics.<br /> Demons must maintain their Cover (their human secret identity) lest it become eroded and expose their location to the hunter-killer angels that pursue them relentlessly. They maintain their Covers by doing things that Cover would do - taking care of its family and kids, doing its day job, walking its dog, all of that. Demons need spiritual Essence to power their supernatural abilities, but can only get it certain ways, many of them physically risky. Demons need to cultivate new Covers in case one of theirs is suddenly blown or exposed, which means going among mortals and making bargains and deals. Demons need to keep an eye on their enemy, if nothing else so they know how close it is to finding them, which means seeking out its lairs and exposing its agents. Every Demon has a long-term goal of achieving Hell - a state of existence where they aren't hunted, either by destroying or reprogramming the God-Machine that hunts them, or by finding a new dimension, or by becoming human for real - and every demon has a Cipher, a four-line riddle that, when solved, guides them on their quest for Hell and can unlock new abilities and insights for the demon. And, of course, this is a White Wolf game, so all the usual politicking and plotting and planning and double-crossing is fair game too.<br /> For once we have a game here where at no point should players ever feel like they have nothing to be doing next. They have a ton of options, and all these things are actually part of the system, not just background or fluff, and working toward these goals gives them real mechanical rewards.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T12:08:12-07:00","id":143770,"title":"","content":"Demon the Descent was an awesome read. Very nice story and soo much scenarios ran through my mind..Its the first book that got me interested in nWoD. Add to that fact while reading it my brain did something of a side project; connecting some non-exsisting dots like &quot;God-Machine = The Computer&quot;, &quot;Angels = Hit Mark 47's&quot;, and &quot;Infrastructure&amp;Occult Matrices = pardigm stablizers to keep the Archmages(cWoD) in deep umbra&quot;, so i subconsiously constructed even a metaplot for my future game :P<br /> <br /> all in all it is a very good game, especially if you like espionage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T15:19:57-07:00","id":143910,"title":"","content":"So, mostly due to Ephsy and Stupid Loserman, I have actually purchased the book and begun reading it. One thing I especially like so far is the sacrifice between cover and compromise for when you attempt to do things.<br /> <br /> This does bring up the point though that most of the games I play with my group are crossover, and based on the descriptions from chapter 1, it seems that playing an unchained would be severely limiting in such a game. Why would they put themselves at risk after all? That, and it seems I would be spending more time per game session rebuilding cover of being paranoid than helping other players.<br /> <br /> Is it possible to have a cover that takes on a more aggressive (almost hunter) personality so that such events help reinforce the cover so long as overt abilities are unused?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T18:16:32-07:00","id":143999,"title":"","content":"Oh, sure. Criminal. Contract killer. Cop \u2014 <i>on the edge.</i> Or make a soul pact with a wizard.<br /> <br /> Two more things to note. The compromise rules don't require you to lose Cover on a failed roll; you can choose instead to accept a glitch if the Cover is too precious. These will stack up over time, but hacking into infrastructure (or other means Storyteller-approved) is stated to allow demons to lose glitches.<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind that compromises occur for acts that are <i>grossly</i> out of character. If a person who knew you in passing would see you do it and know something's not right, that's a compromise. There's a lot of wiggle room there to participate and be useful without running around in Times Square cackling and shooting hellfire out of a shotgun.<br /> <br /> By the way, you can shoot hellfire out of a shotgun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T19:56:33-07:00","id":144031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/142785-sell-me-on-demon?p=143999#post143999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two more things to note. The compromise rules don't require you to lose Cover on a failed roll; you can choose instead to accept a glitch if the Cover is too precious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather, you still lose Cover, but you opt to put a supernatural hole in the identity like speaking in rhyme or being burned by the touch of silver instead of having pinged the Machine's radar in some fashion that will make it harder for you to avoid direct attention from its agents.<br /> <br /> There <i>is,</i> however, a basic power that specifically gives you a buffer for losing Cover due to supernatural nonsense rather than incongruity with the role you've adopted.<br /> <br /> There is also another basic power that lets you put your Cover on low-key autopilot while you do as you please without concern for acting in-character.<br /> <br /> The takeaway from this is that Wheels are very good at their basic job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T20:13:39-07:00","id":144042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/142785-sell-me-on-demon?p=144031#post144031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather, you still lose Cover, but you opt to put a supernatural hole in the identity like speaking in rhyme or being burned by the touch of silver instead of having pinged the Machine's radar in some fashion that will make it harder for you to avoid direct attention from its agents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. The text of the book doesn't make it perfectly clear how much of the failure effect the glitch option is an alternative to. I read it as being an alternative to the full preceding sentence, starting with losing the dot of Cover; a permanent glitch seems like a pretty steep price to pay in comparison if it's just replacing Flagged or the like. Has this question come up on the boards before and gotten an answer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T20:36:01-07:00","id":144052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/142785-sell-me-on-demon?p=144042#post144042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. The text of the book doesn't make it perfectly clear how much of the failure effect the glitch option is an alternative to. I read it as being an alternative to the full preceding sentence, starting with losing the dot of Cover; a permanent glitch seems like a pretty steep price to pay in comparison if it's just replacing Flagged or the like. Has this question come up on the boards before and gotten an answer?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly figured the permanent glitch was because Surveilled and Hunted are rather more serious and difficult to discharge than Shaken or Spooked, but to my recollection the question hasn't come up so far. Given that the effects of Dramatic Failure use a worse set of Conditions or two permanent glitches I feel comfortable assuming that the dot of Cover is lost regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T23:58:53-07:00","id":144229,"title":"","content":"Another thing you could do is: Make Supernaturals be unpredictable on God-Machine's radar. That way, as long as he's with other supernaturals it's harder for him to lose Cover (well for GM to track him, since he's with a bunch of other perception clouding beings).Given how many supernaturals there is this could also explain why GM is making so many mistakes..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T17:19:53-07:00","id":183359,"title":"","content":"I'm still having a hard time getting passed &quot;The Matrix&quot; feel of the game. I've read the quickstart and I'm reading the pre-release of the core book. It just doesn't feel like it belongs in the overall WoD, and since I feel that the God Machine is an unnecessary &quot;update&quot; that muddies the waters of the WoD, I just can't get my head around it. I would really like to play it at least once, so I can have a better idea of how it runs and see if it changes my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3129-topher","name":"Topher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T08:14:44-07:00","id":183807,"title":"","content":"For me &quot;The Matrix&quot; feel of the game fits in perfectly with the World of Darkness and the God-Machine is a perfect aspect for the world. (After all, the idea of Mechanical Angels and a God-Machine were in the original World of Darkness book in the very big early story &quot;Voice of the Angel&quot;. From an OOC perspective, it is the mechanism a storyteller can use to bring more modern conspiracy theories and creepy stories into a reality. Making all legends, new and old, true in the World of Darkness.)<br /> <br /> I perform this thought experiment to get over the machine aspects and realise that Angels and Demons are not robots or programs despite some neat correlations. First, I remove &quot;Machine&quot; from them and see that they follow all the tropes of a fallen angel and a distant God. Next, it is easy to see the Gnostic underpinnings and identify that God as the demiurge (it is actually referred to as this in the new Hunter the Vigil: Mortal Remains book!). A demiurge is as welcome in the World of Darkness as the Circle of Crones pagan gods, or Mage's supernal realms. (In fact, much of Mage was based off of such mysticism).<br /> <br /> Now we look at things about this demiurge. Such as, Biblical text that refers to entities such as the Ophan or Throne and the Cherub. Such creatures are angelic beings, but are profoundly bizarre and not at all the usual, modern trope of a beautiful person, but of a creature of bizarre physics that defies human ideas of how the universe even functions. A wheel with forty-two eyes, and burning with an inner ring of fire, anyone?<br /> <br /> Now that we've looked at Ezekiel's Wheel, and see that even traditional angelic beings are pretty bizarre, we can see that this demiurge behaves oddly. Now we can put the Machine back in God-Machine and realise that the machine was always there. It is bound to the principles of the universe, it is perhaps even the &quot;Clockwork Universe&quot; itself. Mechanisms could be invisible, from the seemingly perfect orbits of the solar system, to the calculated movement of atoms, to the horrible amalgamations of flesh, steel and earth that are this demiurge's most trusted earthly servants; the angels.<br /> <br /> Or so was the run of my mind!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T08:44:42-07:00","id":183844,"title":"","content":"Yeah, people get too caught up on the word &quot;machine&quot; and gear motifs, abd forget that the entire universe does in fact run on what are essentially mechanistic rules. That's what the laws of physics are, the deterministic, mechanical rules that govern everything. And on a slightly more personal scale, humans are quite literally biological machines. Now, in the World of Darkness, symbolism is of utmost importance, so it makes sense that the &quot;God&quot; of such a deterministic universe as the one we live in would be a contraption of metal and gears. Not necessarily because it was actually constructed by industrial means, but because that is the only way our limited minds can comprehend it. Just like Pennywise isn't really a spider, that's just the closest thing to what IT really is that the characters can conceive of. The God-Machine is unquestionably a machine, but it operates on occult matrices and infrastructure and principles we could never hope to understand. So, we conceptualize it as a technological device, because that's something we can understand, and it kind of works the same way if you turn your head sideways and squint hard enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T10:58:16-07:00","id":183885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Topher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/142785-sell-me-on-demon?p=183359#post183359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still having a hard time getting passed &quot;The Matrix&quot; feel of the game. I've read the quickstart and I'm reading the pre-release of the core book. It just doesn't feel like it belongs in the overall WoD, and since I feel that the God Machine is an unnecessary &quot;update&quot; that muddies the waters of the WoD, I just can't get my head around it. I would really like to play it at least once, so I can have a better idea of how it runs and see if it changes my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div> First of all, the God Machine doesn't muddy any waters. That book is basically &quot;Book of Spirits&quot; / &quot;Book of the Dead&quot; / &quot;Inferno,&quot; but for angels instead of spirits, ghosts, or demonic entities, respectively. The God-Machine doesn't exist in Vampire or Werewolf by default. You only include it if you want it included, same as bringing in Infernal demons into Vampire, Mage, Changeling, or whatever. The only game where the GM exists by default is Demon. Everyone else can take it or leave it. <br /> <br /> The GMC RULES are being used to update all the lines, yes. But the first part of the book, that talks about the God Machine? That's entirely optional. <br /> <br /> Two, relax about the whole Matrix thing. People do get hung up on the machine thing too much. Its no different than pushing vampirism as a disease, or genetics determining werewolves, or aliens doubling as Gentry. Super science has always been a thing in the WoD - its just never been front-and-center as much as it is in Demon. But, yes, actually sit down and make a character. Don't even really worry about a game, but seriously make a character in full details. You'd be surprised at how quickly a character feels like a fallen angel. The Exploits and Demon Form especially are thematic - teleporting to magic circles, possession, shadow form, throwing fire from exploits, while wings, horns, tails, hooved feet, red skin, glowing halos and more in Forms. Notice how demons have a weakness to &quot;holy powers&quot; (ie being found / slain by religious followers or angels). Notice how the entire story is a war between Heaven and Hell. <br /> <br /> Also, ignore the Embodiment of Human Sin style of demons. That's really more of Inferno's / Vampire's stick. You are a former angel. Think Fallen (or demon the fallen, if you know it). If you're familiar with League of Legend, read up on Morgana's story. THAT is the type of demon you are playing. <br /> <br /> The Four Incarnations can be seen as fallen angels, imps, devils, and succubi/incubi. Guardians are suggested to start with angelic features, and their powers tend to reflect spiritual abilities and accessing pure knowledge. Destroyers lean towards chaotic powers, fire abilities and animalistic forms - standard tropes for the devil. Messengers are known for their powers of social influences, beautiful forms, and access to succubus-like abilities such as Addiction. Psychopomps specialize in trickery powers, such as shifting their Covers around as well as messing with memories and illusions; in a nutshell, trickster demons are imps. <br /> <br /> Agendas come with four different ways of creating Hell - alternate dimensions where you can &quot;damn&quot; your human friends to, turning Earth itself into your idea of Hell after you kill God and destroy Heaven, or achieving a state of Golconda/Ascension. Or repenting and going back to heaven. All different philosophies for demons you'll find in lots of stories.<br /> <br /> Covers represent a demon's shapeshifting ability. Demons are renowned for appearing as whomever they want to be. Covers allow this, and Mundane embeds let you mess with them even more. Spoofing, perfect memories, and lying are also demonic traits, which have returned in full. These all might have a bit of a science theme tacked on their explanation, but the end result is the same - they're perfect liars, can recall anything, and can take any form and you'll never know. <br /> <br /> Infrastructure, output, occult matrix are all just fancy words for spell components, rituals, and magic results. God Machine magic relies on being in the right place (geomancy), right time when the stars align (astrology), with the right person (magic bloodlines). WoD books have a tendency to use Big Words to make things sound different or more important than these basic concepts really are. <br /> <br /> Check out the example angels - one of them is a being that glows with blinding light, and is weak against weapons forged in absolute darkness. Another is an angel of death, weak to flames. A third is a messenger angel speaking of love, and weak to something dipped in blood. Angels act like angels you read about in stories, and often with a weakness to things we tend to associate with dark powers - darkness, hellfire, and blood magic. <br /> <br /> We can talk about the game, and never once have anything related to machines come up. Its a theme, yes. But one that doesn't really inform the game to a great degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T22:30:50-07:00","id":184547,"title":"","content":"Been talking with one of my friends tonight about the game. We've decided that this game is not for us. It really just seems like it all boils down to playing a rogue computer program. We're going to sit this one out and wait for the conversion guide to bring Fallen up to nWoD rules/mechanics (pre-gm). Thanks for all your input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3129-topher","name":"Topher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}